From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:41:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iommu: apple,dart: describe the clock
 protection slice

On T8132 a power state register of a display power domain is guarded by
a "clock protection" slice in the PS_PROT register bank. While the slice
is enabled, a write that powers the domain's CPU down faults. The native
DART power-down disables the DART's streams, flushes it and then clears
the slice; power-up sets it again.

Add apple,clock-protection to the DART binding: a phandle to the PS_PROT
bank and the DART's slice in it. The bank is shared by several DARTs, so
describe it as a syscon and add its compatible to the syscon binding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4ee2331a5d372305e49b3261c363fa6d8c698511)
(cherry picked from commit e935d56e1cb2e31e2bc68e6e9a294bfe4914895f)
(cherry picked from commit 0706ff36cbbeb2b879bb7a5f2954101073d37bbb)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml       | 13 +++++++++++++
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
index 9ba41ab980..73a3e1764f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
@@ -132,6 +132,19 @@ properties:
       handoff. Linux retains occupied root slots and excludes their entire
       IOVA spans from allocation. This does not assert immutable descendants.
 
+  apple,clock-protection:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
+    items:
+      - items:
+          - description: PS_PROT (clock protection) register bank
+          - description: Index of this DART's slice in the bank
+    description: >
+      The clock protection slice that guards a power state register of the
+      power domain of this DART. Its consumer may power that domain down: the
+      DART's streams are then disabled and flushed, and the slice disabled,
+      before the domain powers off, and the slice is enabled again when it
+      powers up. Only the J713 internal display DARTs use it.
+
   apple,tunable:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
     items:
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
index 945a168b61..4c6bfa4986 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@ properties:
               - apm,xgene-mcb
               - apm,xgene-rb
               - apm,xgene-scu
+              - apple,t8132-ps-prot
               - atmel,sama5d2-sfrbu
               - atmel,sama5d3-nfc-io
               - atmel,sama5d3-sfrbu
